  "title": "What are you doing?",
  "goal": "Say what is going on right now with otyr, dur, ýatyr and ýör, on their own and after -(Y)p.",
  "points": ["gp-yp-progressive"],
  "intro": {
    "text": "*otyr*, *dur*, *ýatyr*, *ýör* are the present of sitting, standing, lying and walking: *Ejäm aşhanada otyr*, my mother is in the kitchen. After a verb in `-(Y)p` they say what is going on: *Ol kitap okap otyr*, she is reading a book; *Ýagyş ýagyp dur*, it's raining. `-ýAr` is always right too.",
    "see": "gp-yp-progressive"
  },
  "vocab": [
    { "tk": "heniz", "en": "still; yet (with a negative)", "pos": "adv", "card": "fc-0139" },
    { "tk": "tomaşa etmek", "en": "to watch (with the dative)", "pos": "verb", "card": "fc-0292" },
    { "tk": "gülmek", "en": "to laugh", "pos": "verb", "card": "fc-0807" },
    { "tk": "aglamak", "en": "to cry", "pos": "verb", "card": "fc-0677" },
    { "tk": "gürleşmek", "en": "to talk (with someone), to chat", "pos": "verb", "card": "fc-0820" }
  ],
